<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">James Bruce</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1730–1794</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> · Also known as James Bruce of Kinnaird</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">James Bruce was a Scottish explorer who spent several years in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ethiopia">Ethiopia</a> and in 1770 reached the source of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/blue-nile">Blue Nile</a> near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lake-tana">Lake Tana</a>. On his return journey in 1772 he passed through <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/funj-sultanate-of-sennar">Sennar</a> and left one of the few eyewitness accounts of the Funj court. His Travels to Discover the Source of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nile">Nile</a>, published in 1790, was widely read though long doubted.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/james-bruce.jpg" alt="James Bruce" width="320" height="385" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Pompeo Batoni · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:James_Bruce.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
